WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.500
Large prompts need structure because the model has to distinguish task instructions from

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:05.000
reference material.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:07.000
Start with a clear task statement.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:11.110
Explain what the model should do, what it should not do, what sources it should rely on,

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:12.975
and what output format is expected.

00:00:12.975 --> 00:00:14.000
When many documents are included,

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:17.370
the first section should help the model understand the job before it sees the raw

00:00:17.370 --> 00:00:18.185
material.

00:00:18.185 --> 00:00:19.995
Source organization is critical.

00:00:19.995 --> 00:00:22.995
Use labels, headings, delimiters, and consistent section names.

00:00:22.995 --> 00:00:27.290
Identify where each excerpt came from and whether it is authoritative, background, draft,

00:00:27.290 --> 00:00:28.975
example, or historical.

00:00:28.975 --> 00:00:32.975
If a prompt contains policy text, implementation notes, and user preferences,

00:00:32.975 --> 00:00:34.975
those categories should not be blended together.

00:00:34.975 --> 00:00:36.995
Clear boundaries reduce ambiguity.

00:00:36.995 --> 00:00:38.995
Priority ordering helps when material conflicts.

00:00:38.995 --> 00:00:40.995
Put controlling instructions before examples.

00:00:40.995 --> 00:00:42.995
Put current requirements before old notes.

00:00:42.995 --> 00:00:45.995
Put summaries before detailed appendices when the summary is trusted.

00:00:45.995 --> 00:00:50.970
Make constraints explicit: required tone, excluded topics, citation expectations,

00:00:50.970 --> 00:00:52.995
formatting rules, and assumptions that should be preserved.

00:00:52.995 --> 00:00:56.250
The model should not have to infer which source has priority.

00:00:56.250 --> 00:00:58.995
Requested output format should be specific.

00:00:58.995 --> 00:01:02.975
A large context prompt can ask for a table, decision memo, checklist, diff summary,

00:01:02.975 --> 00:01:05.200
risk register, or structured JSON-like outline.

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.940
Specific formatting reduces wandering and helps reviewers inspect the result.

00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:10.510
The more material you include,

00:01:10.510 --> 00:01:13.980
the more helpful it is to tell the model exactly how to use that material.
